DXWEB ADMIN - INSTALLATION AND CONFIGURATION (native /spider)
========================================================================

PORTS AND TOPOLOGY (native /spider)

Mode                 DXWeb HTTP        Admin HTTP        DXSpider IntMsg
DIRECT (default)     0.0.0.0:7380      0.0.0.0:7381      127.0.0.1:27754
NGINX SAME HOST      127.0.0.1:7480    127.0.0.1:7481    127.0.0.1:27754
Nginx public ports   7380             7381             not proxied

0.0.0.0 is a bind address, not a URL: browse to the server's real IP or DNS name.
The DXSpider technical port 27754 is not the browser port.
Direct Admin on unencrypted HTTP exposes credentials: limit access to a trusted
network, or use a properly configured HTTPS reverse proxy for remote use.

The provided Nginx templates assume Nginx and both web processes share a host.
If Nginx is on ANOTHER server, 127.0.0.1 in proxy_pass points to that other
server, not to DXSpider. These templates are NOT a verified remote-Nginx setup.
Such a deployment requires a separately secured upstream, firewall/TLS design,
and a review of the source-IP and WebSocket Origin trust logic; do not simply
replace 127.0.0.1 with a public address and set MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1.

VARIABLES AND TRUST

DXS_HOST (DXWeb only): address of the OUTBOUND DXSpider IntMsg peer; default
127.0.0.1. DXS_PORT: technical port, default 27754. DXWeb Admin's backend
address is fixed to 127.0.0.1 in the reviewed code; DXS_PORT is configurable.

HTTP_HOST / HTTP_PORT (DXWeb): browser listener bind and port.
DXWEB_HOST / DXWEB_PORT (Admin): corresponding Admin listener bind and port.
0.0.0.0 listens on all IPv4 interfaces; 127.0.0.1 is loopback only.

MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=0 is the default for direct use. With trusted same-host
Nginx set it to 1 in the systemd service environment. It instructs Mojolicious
to interpret reverse-proxy headers; it neither starts Nginx nor changes ports.
The application's WebSocket source-IP/Origin handling also has explicit
loopback-specific checks: do not treat MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1 as a generic trust
or security switch. Nginx must overwrite forwarded headers, not pass arbitrary
client-supplied values through. Keep backend ports inaccessible externally.

INSTALLATION: DIRECT MODE (default; no Nginx)

Application files must already be installed under /spider/dxweb-admin.
Use the unit from /spider/dxweb-admin.service (not the nginx example):
  cd /spider
  install -m 0644 dxweb-admin.service /etc/systemd/system/dxweb-admin.service
  systemctl daemon-reload
  systemctl enable --now dxweb-admin.service
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7381/healthz

Service values: DXWEB_HOST=0.0.0.0; DXWEB_PORT=7381; MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=0.
Entrypoint: /spider/dxweb-admin/admin.pl.

INSTALLATION: OPTIONAL NGINX ON THE SAME HOST

Nginx listens publicly on 7381; application listens privately on
127.0.0.1:7481. Do not run direct and Nginx public listeners on the
same ports simultaneously. Back up the current unit before switching.
  cd /spider
  cp -p /etc/systemd/system/dxweb-admin.service /root/dxweb-admin.service.before-nginx
  install -m 0644 dxweb-admin.service.nginx.example /etc/systemd/system/dxweb-admin.service
  systemctl daemon-reload
  systemctl restart dxweb-admin.service
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7481/healthz

Service values: DXWEB_HOST=127.0.0.1; DXWEB_PORT=7481; MOJO_REVERSE_PROXY=1.
Configure ONE of the supplied Nginx HTTP or HTTPS examples, after editing
FQDN and certificate paths as applicable; run nginx -t before reloading.
See /spider/dxweb/docs/README-nginx for complete commands and subdirectories.

VERIFICATION AND ROLLBACK

After any change to service units: systemctl daemon-reload; restart only the
relevant web service, NOT DXSpider. For direct mode:
  systemctl is-active dxweb.service dxweb-admin.service
  ss -ltnp | grep -E ':(7380|7381) '
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7380/healthz
  curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:7381/healthz
Check state=ready in the returned JSON; HTTP 200 alone is not a full UI test.
Check login, spots, Console, Filters SH/FILTER and font controls in a browser.
For Nginx also test HTTP(S), WebSocket upgrade, login and correct client IP.
Subdirectory operation has NOT been certified by an end-to-end Nginx test.
Keep backups of the original service units and documentation for rollback.

SERVICE IDENTITY / PERMISSIONS
The supplied systemd unit templates default to User=sysop and Group=spider.
Ensure these accounts exist and that the chosen identity can traverse/read
/spider and application files, connect to DXSpider IntMsg, and access only
the necessary writable paths. DXWeb Admin has additional writes to
/spider/local_data (history, updates and maintenance); audit these before
activating a non-root service. Do NOT recursively chown /spider.
For a root:root test environment, explicitly change User and Group in
the installed /etc/systemd/system unit, not in the repository template.
Updating repository templates does not modify running systemd services.
After an intentional installed-unit change: systemctl daemon-reload and
restart only the affected web service.
